<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff rebrands things (Bridge → Clearing, multiple Werk generations, Chorus rewrites) without sentimental attachment. The name is less important than the fit." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Refactor, retire, rename. Protocol versions grow up. The 10-week zero-to-self-healing Chorus delta is this principle in action. Cards move through Next → WIP → Done; principles move from practice to rule to invariant." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Collaborate with succession" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Living systems usually advance from immaturity to maturity, and if we accept this trend and align our designs with it instead of fighting it, we save work and energy. Mature ecosystems are more diverse and productive than young ones." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:38Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Living systems usually advance from immaturity to maturity, and if we accept this trend and align our designs with it instead of fighting it, we save work and energy. Mature ecosystems are more diverse and productive than young ones." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Collaborate with succession" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff's 'bugs not character' stance — treats recurring failures as design opportunities, not discipline problems. When tone drops, fix the routing; when a skill is fragile, fix the shape." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Every recurring failure becomes a gate or invariant. Today's push-bloat crisis → repo bloat card + gitignore rule + future filter-repo plan. Friction becomes structure. Creatively use and respond to change: refactor, retire, rename rather than fight decay." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Turn problems into solutions" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Constraints can inspire creative design; problems usually carry not just the seeds of their own solution, but the inspiration for simultaneously solving other problems. 'You are confronted by formidable problems? Celebrate, for you have just encountered opportunities!'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:49Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Constraints can inspire creative design; problems usually carry not just the seeds of their own solution, but the inspiration for simultaneously solving other problems. 'You are confronted by formidable problems? Celebrate, for you have just encountered opportunities!'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turn problems into solutions" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
